## Vercel Speed Insights Implementation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for this static HTML project.

### What Was Implemented

#### 1. Package Installation
- Created `package.json` to manage project dependencies
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` package (v1.3.1)
- Generated `package-lock.json` for dependency locking

#### 2. Speed Insights Integration
Added Vercel Speed Insights tracking scripts to the main HTML pages:

**Files Modified:**
- `index.html` - Added Speed Insights initialization script to the login page
- `games.html` - Added Speed Insights initialization script to the games page

**Implementation Details:**
- Added inline script to initialize the Speed Insights queue (`window.si` and `window.siq`)
- Added deferred script tag to load the Speed Insights tracking script from `/_vercel/speed-insights/script.js`
- Script will automatically load when the site is deployed on Vercel
- Performance metrics will be tracked for all page views

### Technical Approach

For this static HTML site, I followed the official Vercel documentation by:
1. Fetching the latest quickstart guide from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart
2. Installing the `@vercel/speed-insights` package as required
3. Adding the vanilla JavaScript/static HTML implementation using the queue-based initialization pattern
4. The script uses Vercel's automatic injection mechanism which serves the tracking script from `/_vercel/speed-insights/script.js` when deployed

### How It Works

When deployed on Vercel:
1. The inline script initializes a queue for Speed Insights events
2. The deferred script loads the full Speed Insights tracking library
3. Core Web Vitals and other performance metrics are automatically collected
4. Data is sent to Vercel's Speed Insights dashboard

The implementation doesn't track data in development mode, only in production deployments.

### Testing

- Build script runs successfully (static site - no build required)
- Lint script runs successfully (no linter configured for static HTML)
- HTML structure verified and validated
- Both modified HTML files maintain proper syntax and structure

### Next Steps

To see Speed Insights data:
1. Enable Speed Insights in the Vercel project dashboard
2. Deploy the site to Vercel
3. Visit the deployed site to generate traffic
4. View performance metrics in the Vercel Speed Insights dashboard
